<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greater Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> was a state created in September 1945 in the American zone of occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It combined the parts of the People's State of Hesse east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> with most of the former Prussian province of Hesse-Nassau. After its constitution was approved by referendum in December 1946 it was renamed Hesse, now one of the states of the Federal Republic of Germany.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greater-hesse.jpg" alt="Greater Hesse" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 52 Pickup · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map-GreaterHesse.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
